  {
   "sid": "s4",
   "date": "2026-05-14",
   "url": "https://www.justice.gov/opa/speech/acting-deputy-assistant-attorney-general-criminal-enforcement-daniel-gladd-delivers",
   "text": "Our detection capability does not diminish when conduct migrates to software. It grows. Because the paper trail does not disappear. It multiplies. Every automated bid is a structured record. Every tool that ingests competitor-data inputs is an artifact. Every query to a language-model-based pricing or bidding assistant leaves a log.",
